-- title:
--   Prime-to-p toric points as Hom(ℤ[SS]⁰,μ_m)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; let $\Lambda$ be level data at $A$ (a structural morphism $\sigma_A\colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ compatible with the generic point, a scheme with relative group law, and identifications of its generic and special points with $J_H(M/p)$ and with the glued $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the reduced function field) and let $O$ be a Néron object over it, so a smooth separated group scheme $O.g$ with $O.\mathrm{pts}\colon J_H(M,H) \simeq$ generic points, $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ on special points, toric rank, gluing set $O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ (a finite set of pairs of places of the reduced function field) and toric lift. Let $m > 0$ be coprime to $p$, and assume that every family $\bar w\colon O.\mathrm{ssFinset} \to \mathrm{Additive}\,\kappa^\times$ of node units whose class $\mathrm{nodeUnit}(\bar w)$ in the glued $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ vanishes is constant. Then there is an isomorphism of additive groups $e$ from $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup of $J_H(M,H)$ generated by the toric points $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$, onto $\operatorname{Hom}(X, \mathrm{Additive}\,\mu_m(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}))$, where $X = \mathrm{characterLattice}\,O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ is the kernel of the total-degree map on $\mathbb{Z}^{O.\mathrm{ssFinset}}$, with three properties. First, $e$ is pinned by reduction: for every $A$-algebra map $\chi$ from $\mathrm{muCoord}\,A\,(O.\mathrm{toricRank})\,m$ to $A$ and every $\bar w$ such that $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{residue} \circ \chi$, followed by the toric lift, followed by the first pullback projection of $O.g$ along $\Lambda.\sigma_A$, equals the morphism underlying $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}(\mathrm{nodeUnit}(\bar w))$, the point $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$ at $\chi$ pushed into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, and for each $a \in X$ there is $u \in A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the root of unity $\mathrm{toMul}(e(x)(a))$ and whose residue is $\mathrm{evalHom}\,a\,(\mathrm{toMul} \circ \bar w) = \prod_s \bar w(s)^{a(s)}$. Second, such a $\bar w$ exists for every $\chi$. Third, equivariance in transposed form: if $\varphi$ is an endomorphism of $O.g$ over the base which is additive for the relative group law, $f$ is a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear endomorphism of $X$ and $op$ an additive endomorphism of node data which are adjoint for the evaluation pairing ($\mathrm{evalHom}(f a)(w) = \mathrm{evalHom}(a)(op\,w)$), $\varphi$ carries $\mathrm{ptsSp}(\mathrm{nodeUnit}(w))$ to $\mathrm{ptsSp}(\mathrm{nodeUnit}(op\,w))$, and the restriction of $\varphi$ to the fibre along $\Lambda.\sigma_A$ is compatible through the toric lift with some endomorphism $\psi$ of $\mathrm{muStr}$, then for every $x \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ the point obtained by composing $O.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ with $\varphi$ again lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ and its image under $e$ is $e(x) \circ f$.
--
--   This is the formal counterpart of the description of the prime-to-$p$ torsion of the toric part of the special fibre of the Jacobian at level $\Gamma_H(M)$ with $p \mid M$: the character group of the torus is the degree-zero lattice on the set of gluing (supersingular) pairs, and the $m$-torsion of the torus is its $\mu_m$-dual, with endomorphisms acting through the transpose of their action on the lattice. It is used in the computation of the order of the toric and finite parts of the $m$-torsion and in identifying the action of the $U_p$-type operator on toric points with the cyclotomic character modulo $m$.
